.TH GDIAGRAM 1 "February 2026" "gDiagram 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gdiagram \- GTK4 diagram viewer and editor for PlantUML and Mermaid
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gdiagram
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIFILE\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gdiagram
is a native Linux diagram viewer and editor supporting PlantUML and Mermaid
syntax. It renders diagrams natively using Graphviz (no Java required) with
real-time preview, click-to-source navigation, and headless export.

When invoked with a \fIFILE\fR and no \fB\-\-export\fR option, the file is
opened in the graphical editor. When \fB\-\-export\fR is specified, gdiagram
runs headless and writes the rendered output to the given path.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-export " " \fIOUTPUT\fR
Export the diagram to \fIOUTPUT\fR and exit (headless mode). Requires a
\fIFILE\fR argument. The output format is controlled by \fB\-\-format\fR.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Set the export format. Supported values:
.RS
.TP
.B png
Portable Network Graphics (default)
.TP
.B svg
Scalable Vector Graphics
.TP
.B pdf
Portable Document Format
.TP
.B dot
Graphviz DOT source (useful for debugging)
.RE
.TP
.B \-\-scale
Scale the PNG output to 71.5% of its native Graphviz size, matching the
visual dimensions of PlantUML-rendered diagrams. Requires
.BR \-\-format " png"
(or the default png format). Uses ImageMagick
.BR convert (1)
with a Lanczos filter.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Enable verbose debug output. Prints parser diagnostics, render timings, and
GLib debug messages to standard output.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a brief usage summary and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version string and exit.
.SH FILE FORMATS
.TP
.B .puml
PlantUML source. Supports sequence, class, activity, state, component,
deployment, use-case, object, ER, Gantt, mind-map, JSON, YAML, timing,
nwdiag, Archimate, and chronology diagrams.
.TP
.B .mmd
Mermaid source. Supports flowchart, sequence, state, class, ER, Gantt, pie,
user journey, git graph, mindmap, timeline, quadrant, XY chart, kanban,
sankey, requirement, block, packet, C4, architecture, ZenUML, radar, and
treemap diagrams.
.PP
File format is auto-detected from the extension and from content keywords,
so either extension works for either format.
.SH EXAMPLES
Open a diagram in the GUI:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gdiagram diagram.puml
gdiagram diagram.mmd
.fi
.RE
.PP
Export a PlantUML sequence diagram to PNG:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gdiagram diagram.puml \-e output.png
.fi
.RE
.PP
Export a Mermaid flowchart to SVG:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gdiagram flowchart.mmd \-e out.svg \-f svg
.fi
.RE
.PP
Export to PNG scaled to PlantUML dimensions:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gdiagram diagram.puml \-e output.png \-\-scale
.fi
.RE
.PP
Export the raw DOT source for inspection:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gdiagram diagram.puml \-e diagram.dot \-f dot
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Export failed (parse error, rendering error, or I/O error).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR dot (1),
.BR convert (1)
